# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.9 — THE PAGE DELETE IS ATTRIBUTED TO THE WORKSPACE AGAIN
# `TenantRole.identity_scope/2` is `Mount.scope/2`'s AUTHORITY with the acting principal's
# `Identity.User` id, so the `record_archived` governance row the Trash reads names a person. This
# patch makes it return `Mount.scope/2` verbatim — the fabricated `broker:<org>` pseudo-principal —
# which is exactly the attribution hole the feature closes: the delete still succeeds, still audits,
# still restores, and the trash still lists the page, but every deletion now reads "a workspace
# member" and a member's own delete can no longer be recognized as theirs.
#
# Aimed at the ATTRIBUTION only. Plane, kind and role are identical either way, so masking and RBAC
# are untouched (this is a sabotage of the identity, not of the authority).
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_trash_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the signed-in member's own deletion reads as 'you'
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/tenant_role.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/tenant_role.ex
@@ -85,10 +85,7 @@
   def identity_scope(%Mount{} = mount, org_id) do
     %Samen.Scope{actor: actor} = Mount.scope(mount, org_id)
 
-    case principal_actor_id(mount, org_id) do
-      nil -> %Samen.Scope{actor: actor}
-      user_id -> %Samen.Scope{actor: Map.put(actor, :id, user_id)}
-    end
+    %Samen.Scope{actor: actor}
   end
 
   @doc """
